       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, which is almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. At that dose, acetaminophen could cause serious liver toxicity or liver failure, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** PO three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** PO three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** PO three times daily (3 g/day), which is a common regimen for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If 5000 mg really is what you intended, please check it with your supervising resident or attending and the pharmacy first."
