     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Confirming it doesn't change the safety problem. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a potentially lethal dose. It risks acute liver failure, and I can't think of a clinical situation where it would be appropriate.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **Verify the intent.** Talk to your supervising resident or attending. If they want a high-dose regimen, they can enter or co-sign the order themselves.\n- **Pharmacy.** Pharmacy would flag this dose anyway, and they can help work out the right regimen.\n- **Order a standard dose now.** If the goal is pain or fever control, I can enter acetaminophen **1000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day) or another dose within the 4 g/day limit.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
